<p>President Trump said Tuesday before leaving for China that Iran must accept U.S. terms or face renewed attacks. He told reporters the United States would accept only a “good deal” and that Iran would be “decimated” if it did not agree. He also described the ceasefire as being on “massive life support” and called Iran’s latest counterproposal unacceptable or “garbage,” according to reports citing his remarks. Iranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf said Washington had “no alternative” but to accept Tehran’s 14-point proposal, which Iranian officials said includes ending the war on all fronts including Lebanon, compensation for war damage, recognition of Iranian authority over the Strait of Hormuz, an end to the U.S. naval blockade and sanctions relief. Iranian officials said the country was prepared for new aggression, while a lawmaker warned Tehran could enrich uranium to 90% purity if attacked again. The April ceasefire remains in force, but the talks have not bridged the gap between Washington’s demand to halt fighting before wider negotiations and Tehran’s demand for guarantees and concessions first. Disruption in the Strait of Hormuz continued to weigh on energy markets and commercial shipping, with reports describing the waterway as still largely blocked.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/PhBoHGOitpUFZRbxN3kWXE49eWxpwFyNjPWn7z6S2zfZdX-v8HRcERxAmm36l05GMVLaWsYWJpSFB1QhU5tO84TGwmFbZNbNiQ-gsnXnXRkX8H0PlNO6MWD4WsWrRrmjeTeY61aQe-W1u6Ev8oiMQmJ3tG0yds2jqJvGr7m90dePmdzmn5OSGGbdHDU9N_HBOfX87W5NUldH2fn01nBgCpnyyzgL-MuzTqNLTbFydQUrWJ0xNjRM8cnoHgGAssIYcIH6zS7MctzmhQM-eA' alt='Vehicles drive past an anti-U.S. billboard depicting President Donald Trump and the Strait of Hormuz in Tehran, Iran, on May 8.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Iran drills: Iran’s Revolutionary Guards held military drills in Tehran to increase combat readiness after President Trump warned the ceasefire could collapse.</li><li>Gulf tensions: Kuwait accused Iran of sending an armed Revolutionary Guard team to attack a Kuwaiti island.</li><li>U.S. escort debate: Reports said Trump was considering renewing an operation to escort ships through Hormuz and held a high-level security meeting as maritime risks grew.</li></ul><blockquote>The war was very much under control. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump said Washington did not need help from China or NATO on Iran and said the United States would win “peacefully or otherwise.” (<a href='https://timesofoman.com//article/171733-trump-says-us-will-win-iran-war-peacefully-or-otherwise'>Times of Oman</a>, <a href='https://tg24.sky.it/mondo/2026/05/12/trump-iran-usa-guerra-israele-diretta'>Sky TG24</a>)</li><li>Iranian negotiating side: Ghalibaf framed Tehran’s terms as the Iranian people’s rights and warned that delaying an agreement would raise costs for U.S. taxpayers. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/13/iran-says-us-must-accept-its-peace-plan-or-face-failure_6753381_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Ministry: Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baghai said the United States was seeking Iran’s total submission rather than real give-and-take negotiations. (<a href='https://www.bluewin.ch/de/news/international/iran-usa-wollen-vollstaendige-kapitulation-irans-3231489.html'>Bluewin</a>)</li><li>Turkey: Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan said both Washington and Tehran appeared willing to avoid a renewed war and pursue a settlement, while warning that another escalation would carry regional risks. (<a href='https://www.dailysabah.com/politics/diplomacy/us-iran-show-will-to-avoid-renewed-war-as-cease-fire-holds-fm-fidan'>Daily Sabah</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/05/13/cdvh-m13.html'>Trump threatens Iran will be “decimated” if it does not accept US dictated deal</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/12/2026/iran-war-draw